Thanksgiving Day has sported NFL games since the league&#x2019;s inception in 1920, and now Turkey Day tussles on the gridiron are supercharged for the streaming future.

On Nov. 25, Netflix and the NFL would like football fans to join them for a new holiday tradition: the Thanksgiving Eve game. And like the streamer&#x2019;s Christmas Day gridiron matchups, this one is A-list all the way: the Los Angeles Rams vs. the Green Bay Packers at L.A.&#x2019;s SoFi Stadium and a halftime show headlined by U2. blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-variety-article-mid-article-uid0' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid-article1","mid-articleX","mid","mid-article"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article") .addSize([[300,250],[2,2],[300,251],[2,4],[4,2],[320,480],[620,366],[300,450]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; }); Related Stories 'Grendel' Animated Series Set at Netflix From 'Widow's Bay' Writer Years After Live-Action Adaptation Was Scrapped 'Russell Brand: Open Secret' Director Says Finding Contributors Wasn't Easy: 'There's Been a Landscape of Fear'

Gabe Spitzer, Netflix&#x2019;s VP of global live sports and entertainment, says that cooking up a Thanksgiving Eve game came naturally between Netflix and the NFL. The partners have had great success in the last two years with Christmas Day games, with the matchups hitting 30 million-plus global viewers per game. The focus on showcasing games during holiday periods has conditioned Netflix subscribers and football fans to think of the streamer as a place for out-of-the-ordinary games.

&#x201C;As the NFL opened up more inventory and started talking to us about [possibly adding] more games, [Thanksgiving Eve] is one that they mentioned and immediately it felt like the perfect fit,&#x201D; says Spitzer, who spoke with Variety while sporting a New England Patriots cap.

Onnie Bose, the NFL&#x2019;s VP of broadcasting, echoes that sentiment. The league has learned &#x201C;over the last few years that when family and friends are together, they gravitate toward watching our games,&#x201D; Bose says. &#x201C;Our Thanksgiving viewership has always been strong. I think it&#x2019;s exploded. We hit 57 million viewers with the Kansas City-Dallas game last year.&#x201D; blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-dsk-tab-mid-article2-uid1' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid","mid-article2","mid-articleX"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article2") .addSize([[320,480],[300,250],[300,251],[2,4],[4,2],[620,366],[300,450]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

There is precedent for staking out new NFL-watching traditions, as the league has worked closely with Amazon Prime Video over the last few years to successfully establish the Black Friday game on the day after Thanksgiving.

"We've been building Black Friday with Amazon over the last few years. So Thanksgiving is a clear natural weekend where people are together,&#x201D; Bose says. "They're watching football. We&#x2019;ve seen that on Christmas also in the last few years. We just looked at it as an opportunity to do something new.&#x201D;

It&#x2019;s been a fruitful marriage between the NFL, which has wants to expand the popularity of football around the world, and the streaming giant with its global footprint in 190 countries. For Thanksgiving Eve, NBC Sports is producing the game broadcast; EverWonder Studio is serving as executive producer for Netflix. Jesse Collins Entertainment, the banner known for handling the Emmy Awards, Oscars and Super Bowl Halftime show, is producing U2&#x2019;s halftime performance.

Netflix's expanded agreement with the NFL runs through the 2029 season, with a growing presence across the NFL calendar, from Week 1 through Super Bowl week.

This year, Netflix streamed the first-ever NFL game played in Australia, a matchup between the San Francisco 49ers and the Los Angeles Rams, on Sept. 10. The NFL also played games in London, Madrid, Munich, Rio de Janeiro, Paris and Mexico City this year. Live sports are a coveted draw for broadcasters and streamers alike. In the U.S., through the Nov. 22 matchup, the NFL has averaged 18.2 million viewers across its broadcasts, its highest mid-season number since 2010.

Netflix&#x2019;s partnership with the league includes Christmas Day games, the NFL's first regular-season game in Australia, the Thanksgiving Eve game, a Week 18 matchup and the annual NFL Honors awards ceremony.

This week&#x2019;s game marks Netflix&#x2019;s second time working with the L.A. Rams this season.

&#x201C;Our experience working with Netflix has been fantastic. There is a shared commitment between the Rams and Netflix to put fans first and deliver an exceptional experience, both inside SoFi Stadium in Inglewood, and for audiences watching around the globe,&#x201D; says Kathryn Kai-ling Frederick, chief marketing officer for the Rams. &#x201C;Netflix brings a unique ability to combine world-class storytelling, entertainment and live sports, creating opportunities to reach new audiences and elevate the way fans engage with the game. We&#x2019;re excited to continue building on our relationship and collaborate on moments that extend beyond the field.&#x201D; blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-variety-article-mid-articleX-uid2' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["btf","mid-articleX","mid"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-articleX") .addSize([[320,480],[300,250],[300,251],[620,366]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

The strategy with the NFL is to create lasting moments and cement Netflix in the viewers&#x2019; minds as a marquee destination for top games and entertainment. &#x201C;We're not the networks that have hundreds of games a year. We're really showing up intentionally at a few points across the season, and I think this is where Thanksgiving Eve fits in perfectly,&#x201D; Spitzer says. &#x201C;We're that opening game, an international game in Melbourne, Thanksgiving Eve, two games on Christmas and then that final weekend of the season when stakes are all on the line for some of these potential playoff teams.&#x201D;

The Rams and Packers, both with a record of 6-4, are each fighting for a spot in the playoffs, which means that Wednesday&#x2019;s game has big consequences for both teams&#x2019; seasons.

Bose says that the Netflix partnership was a natural for the NFL&#x2019;s plans, especially after seeing how the streamer brought the spotlight to its Christmas Day games.

&#x201C;They&#x2019;ve truly embraced Christmas. They&#x2019;ve made it into a big event with their double headers. It&#x2019;s worldwide distribution. They&#x2019;ve engaged in putting on concerts,&#x201D; Bose says. "There's not a lot of places where we can add new windows where we have partners that are well established in certain places. This was a new window. It fits with their strategy of wanting to have kind of events and standalone windows that resonate.&#x201D;

Spitzer says that Netflix approaches its live events with an eye to setting a high bar in the pop culture landscape. It did that in 2024 with the &#x201C;Beyonc&#xE9; Bowl&#x201D; during the Houston Texans-Baltimore Ravens Christmas Day game, which drew some 27 million viewers in the U.S., not to mention the social media conversation generated by her performance. Beyonce's revue included Shaboozey, the Texas Southern University&#x2019;s Oceans of Soul Marching band and a wide range of performers that spoke to Southern Black and Latin history and music.

In 2025, Snoop Dogg&#x2019;s halftime show for Netflix&#x2019;s Christmas Day games drew 29 million viewers and featured country superstar Lainey Wilson and the hitmakers of &#x201C;K-pop Demon Hunters&#x201D;: EJAE, Audrey Nuna and Rei Ami.

&#x201C;Obviously, we&#x2019;re so early in our live sports journey, but it was a great start,&#x201D; Spitzer says.

With U2, Netflix aims to create another big moment with a band that&#x2019;s a household name worldwide. &#x201C;They've only done it twice,&#x201D; Spitzer says about the rock superstars' NFL game appearances. U2 played in the 2002 game in a moving set that was also a tribute to the victims of 9/11; the other was as an opening act on &#x201C;Monday Night Football&#x201D; in 2006 as part of the reopening of the Louisiana Superdome a year after the devastation of Hurricane Katrina. &#x201C;They want to be a part of a big moment, and we're thrilled that they want to be on Netflix for launching this new tradition as well,&#x201D; Spitzer says. blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-variety-article-mid-articleX-uid3' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["btf","mid-articleX","mid"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-articleX") .addSize([[320,480],[300,250],[300,251],[620,366]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

The streamer is also bringing celebrity chef David Chang aboard in the pregame show to spotlight food, tailgating and other game-day traditions. For Netflix, it&#x2019;s as much of a live event strategy as it is a sports strategy.

&#x201C;It&#x2019;s about creating that new fandom. We want to create those global water cooler moments,&#x201D; says Spitzer. &#x201C;That could be a big boxing match. It could be NFL games. It could be the Women&#x2019;s World Cup, or it could be Alex Honnold climbing a 101-story building. If we&#x2019;re going to do a big live event, we really want to make sure it cuts through.&#x201D;

Netflix has the rights to the 2027 and 2031 FIFA Women&#x2019;s World Cup, so lessons learned staging NFL games and other live events look to culminate next year in Brazil. Spitzer won&#x2019;t comment on whether the streamer is bidding for the 2030 and 2024 Men&#x2019;s World Cup rights.

The Women&#x2019;s World Cup is &#x201C;the most ambitious project that we&#x2019;ve ever done. Thirty straight days, 64 matches over eight hours a day in the U.S. and Canada,&#x201D; Spitzer says. &#x201C;We&#x2019;ve been planning it for two years. There&#x2019;s nothing bigger, so we can&#x2019;t wait for that.&#x201D;

For Netflix, aligning with the biggest brand in U.S. sports &#x2014; the NFL &#x2014; and creating a new tradition is good for driving global subscriptions and good for the bottom line in a business that has seen layoffs and management shake-ups like every other content giant. For the next few weeks, Team Netflix is all about driving viewership to Thanksgiving Eve and Christmas Day action on the gridiron.

&#x201C;We want to create a new family tradition with Netflix,&#x201D; Spitzer says. "It's really about bringing fans together for the biggest moments in sports.&#x201D;

&#x201C; The Seven Madmen ,&#x201D; starring Selton Mello (&#x201C;I&#x2019;m Still Here&#x201D;) and directed by Benjam&#xED;n Naishtat, is wrapping its shoot in Buenos Aires on Nov. 24, marking the latest advance on a production that weighs in as one of Latin America&#x2019;s big bets for A-List festival selection in 2027.

A present day noir thriller loosely adapting Argentinean novelist Robert Arlt&#x2019;s 1929 and 1931 modern classic novels &#x201C;The Seven Madmen&#x201D; and &#x201C;The Flamethrowers,&#x201D; the movie also reps the latest feature from Argentina&#x2019;s Naishtat (&#x201C;Rojo,&#x201D; &#x201C;Puan,&#x201D; &#x201C;Glaxo&#x201D;) who is fast consolidating as one of Latin America&#x2019;s major auteurs. blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-variety-article-mid-article-uid0' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid-article1","mid-articleX","mid","mid-article"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article") .addSize([[300,250],[2,2],[300,251],[2,4],[4,2],[320,480],[620,366],[300,450]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; }); Related Stories ‘Russell Brand: Open Secret’: Netflix Doc Reveals His ‘Jokes’ About Rape, Making a Girlfriend ‘Brush Her Teeth Until They Bled’ and More ‘Bad Day’ Trailer: Cameron Diaz Is a Single Mom Who Accidentally Robs a Bank in Netflix Comedy

Naishtat also forms part of a loose knit but burgeoning new generation of Spanish-language cineastes (think Spain&#x2019;s Rodrigo Sorogoyen) that have a clear sense of film genre and combine bold visuals with a large concern for contemporary social issues.

&#x201C;The Seven Madmen&#x201D; also stars Martin Piroyansky (&#x201C;Porno y helado&#x201D;). Arlt&#x2019;s novel of the same time turned on young Remo Erdosian who&#x2019;s threatened with imprisonment unless he returns money he&#x2019;s stolen. He seeks out Alberto, a mysterious Astrologer, who promises to help Remo if in return the young man joins his organization which, he discovers, aims to overthrow the government.

Just how much of that get into Naishtat&#x2019;s film, given it is also inspired by &#x201C;The Flamethrowers,&#x201D; remains to be seen with its producers keeping its plot under wraps, describing it as &#x201C;set in a twisted Buenos Aires&#x201D; and &#x201C;an intense thriller.&#x201D; It is known, however, that Piroyansky plays Remo and Mello the Astrologer. blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-dsk-tab-mid-article2-uid1' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid","mid-article2","mid-articleX"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article2") .addSize([[320,480],[300,250],[300,251],[2,4],[4,2],[620,366],[300,450]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

&#x201C;Benjam&#xED;n is a deeply inspiring filmmaker,&#x201D; Mello told Variety . &#x201C;It is an honor to have been invited by him to bring to life one of the most iconic characters in Argentine literature: El Astr&#xF3;logo, created by Roberto Arlt and now reimagined by Benjam&#xED;n in the film we are making together.&#x201D;

Mello added: &#x201C;I have been experiencing something new: a sense of Latin American belonging that moves me deeply while also expanding my artistic expression. This project has brought about an intimate celebration of a rare and very special moment in my journey."

Cast is rounded up by Lorena Vega (&#x201C;Envious&#x201D;), Diego Cremonesi, Sof&#xED;a Morandi, Andrea Frigerio, Iv&#xE1;n Gonz&#xE1;lez, Paula Grinszpan and Lola Berthet, with Carla Peterson (&#x201C;27 Nights&#x201D;) and special guest star Mercedes Mor&#xE1;n (&#x201C;The Kingdom&#x201D;).

"Ever since I first read &#x2018;The Seven Madmen,&#x2019; I have been captivated by its dark beauty, by its characters who exist beyond the reach of any law, and by its ability to capture Buenos Aires in a way perhaps no other book ever has,&#x201D; said Naishtat.

He added that he had spent &#x201C;more than 10 years&#x201D; working on an adaptation which he knew was &#x201C;impossible, which, in a way, came as a relief, since my interpretation is decidedly free.&#x201D;

&#x201C;At the darkest moment in Argentine cinema, devastated by a government hostile to any form of cultural expression, an eclectic group of producers from around the world, an extraordinary cast, and a world-class crew joined forces to make this project a reality.&#x201D;

In an era where Latin American films of late ambition can only be made with streaming service support or multi-lateral co-production, the &#x201C;eclectic group&#x201D; referred to by Naishtat takes in Argentina&#x2019;s P&#xFA;cara Cine, founded by Federico Eibuszyc, which produced Naishtat&#x2019;s &#x201C;The Movement,&#x201D; &#x201C;Rojo&#x201D; and &#x201C;Pu&#xE1;n&#x201D; and Pasto, founded by B&#xE1;rbara Francisco Mendivilm which teamed with P&#xFA;cara to produce &#x201C;Puan.&#x201D;

They are joined by &#x201C;Argentina 1985&#x201D; producer Infinity Hill , Particular Crowd (&#x201C;The Extortion&#x201D;) and Brazilian production companies MyMama Entertainment (&#x201C;Medusa&#x201D;) and Bubbles Project (&#x201C;Elephants in the Fog,&#x201D;) and Ecce Films (France), Materia Cinema (Spain), and Pandora Films (Germany), in association with Bord Cadre and Sula Films. blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-variety-article-mid-articleX-uid2' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["btf","mid-articleX","mid"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-articleX") .addSize([[320,480],[300,250],[300,251],[620,366]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

It is no coincidence that two novels published in 1929 and 1931, an era of social fanaticism which saw the rise of fascism, are now set to receive a free present-day adaptation.

&#x201C;Revisiting the unclassifiable marvel that Roberto Arlt published in 1929 is a timely endeavor in order to decipher the Argentinian and planetary present, said Naishtat.

Noted Particular Crowd President Peter Bevan: &#x201D;&#x2019;The Seven Madmen&#x2019; pulsates with relentless tension, singular humor and Benjam&#xED;n Naishtat&#x2019;s signature lucidity.&#x201D;

